WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:02.161
AI safety research.

2
00:00:02.161 --> 00:00:04.167
The Anthropic Residency map.

3
00:00:04.467 --> 00:00:06.460
In November twenty twenty six,

4
00:00:06.460 --> 00:00:12.442
Anthropic opened a paid research residency for professors, founders, and senior engineers.

5
00:00:12.442 --> 00:00:15.100
No machine learning background required.

6
00:00:16.300 --> 00:00:18.800
Why does a job post matter for a study plan?

7
00:00:19.100 --> 00:00:25.033
Because it names exactly which research areas a frontier lab wants a non-AI person to grow into.

8
00:00:25.333 --> 00:00:28.567
Most of them sit one step past interpretability.

9
00:00:29.767 --> 00:00:33.525
Scalable oversight keeps a model honest when it outdoes you.

10
00:00:33.525 --> 00:00:37.533
Debate, weak to strong generalization, and catching sandbagging.

11
00:00:37.833 --> 00:00:43.204
AI control assumes the model may try to cause harm, and makes deployment safe anyway.

12
00:00:43.204 --> 00:00:46.300
A trusted smaller model watches the stronger one.

13
00:00:46.600 --> 00:00:49.825
Model organisms are small models built to misbehave,

14
00:00:49.825 --> 00:00:54.167
so alignment faking and subliminal learning can be studied in the lab.

15
00:00:54.467 --> 00:00:57.912
Model internals means probes on activations, steering,

16
00:00:57.912 --> 00:01:01.167
persona vectors, and chain of thought faithfulness.

17
00:01:01.467 --> 00:01:06.610
Safeguards research covers constitutional classifiers and auditing agents.

18
00:01:06.610 --> 00:01:12.100
ML systems covers how frontier models are trained, down to the RL environments.

19
00:01:13.300 --> 00:01:16.100
Four concepts were missing from this site until now.

20
00:01:16.400 --> 00:01:21.497
AI control, model organisms, chain of thought faithfulness, and AI welfare.

21
00:01:21.497 --> 00:01:26.867
Frontier red teaming for cyber, robotics, and cryptography rounds out the list.

22
00:01:28.067 --> 00:01:31.667
The good news: every area builds on something you already studied.

23
00:01:31.967 --> 00:01:34.722
RLHF and DPO lead to oversight.

24
00:01:34.722 --> 00:01:37.300
Red teaming leads to control.

25
00:01:37.600 --> 00:01:40.129
Fine tuning leads to model organisms.

26
00:01:40.129 --> 00:01:44.367
Attention and sparse autoencoders lead to probes and steering.

27
00:01:45.567 --> 00:01:48.667
Three weekend builds cover most of the vocabulary.

28
00:01:48.967 --> 00:01:52.918
Train a linear probe on a small open model and steer with it.

29
00:01:52.918 --> 00:01:56.610
Build a trusted monitor that flags an agent's tool calls.

30
00:01:56.610 --> 00:02:01.533
Fine tune a model organism, then try to find the habit with an audit script.

31
00:02:02.733 --> 00:02:03.567
To recap.

32
00:02:03.867 --> 00:02:09.474
The residency is paid, needs no ML background, and closes November twenty second.

33
00:02:09.474 --> 00:02:12.867
Eight areas, most one step past interpretability.

34
00:02:13.167 --> 00:02:16.820
Learn control, model organisms, faithfulness, and welfare.

35
00:02:16.820 --> 00:02:21.167
Then do the three builds and read Anthropic's recommended directions.
